{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1336854-which-has-been-your-favourite-area-of-3e-creation-how-different-did-the-games-feel","id":1336854,"title":"Which has been your favourite area of 3e Creation? How different did the games feel?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Exalted"],"posts":[{"date":"2019-09-19T06:42:00-07:00","id":1336854,"title":"Which has been your favourite area of 3e Creation? How different did the games feel?","content":"My survey of where people had played got:<br /> 10 games in the North<br /> 5 games in the North-East<br /> 1 or 2 in the East proper<br /> 12 in the Scavenger Lands<br /> 11 in the South-East, 9 of them around the Dreaming Sea.<br /> 6 in the South<br /> 7 or 8 in the South-West<br /> 8 in the West<br /> And a few in other places; 1 in Autocthon, 1 in Gloam, 1 on the Blessed Isle.<br /> <br /> But about half of people are actually on there two or three times, as they'd played different games in different areas. So I was wondering which you liked most, and how different areas affected the nature of the game.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-09-19T07:45:46-07:00","id":1336866,"title":"","content":"Favourite was probably the Blessed Isle, although that was only about two sessions of a six session mortal game. A group of mortals, including an unexalted Dynast, were sent to the North on a mission by Nellens Poramo, except one of his political enemies thought it was some kind of bid for more power so they sent an exalted assassin after them, and taking advantage of the rise in banditry to the North of the Isle they...anyway I liked it. Then the game went to the super far north and became a desolate horror game.<br /> <br /> I think the worst one was the West game, just because lots of us were really hyped for the sailing and naval combat but that really fell short for us. We never really got that sense of adventure I was looking for but I can\u2019t really articulate why that may be. I will say that having a boat that gave us easy access to many separated island cultures was cool though.<br /> <br /> The far far north east game was fun in that it was so far from any Dragonblooded power that we could afford to be a lot more cavalier with our essence and artifacts. It also had a very dynamic range of seasons like Canada and the northern US, so we could have blistering summers and frigid winters, which was pretty cool. It also gave us a chance to develop cultures relatively unaffected by the shadow of the Scarlett Empire.<br /> <br /> Exact opposite of that, the south game took place IN a satrapy, so the PCs had to be pretty careful most of the time. I liked the aesthetics I got to pull from there, the Alin from Rise of Legends mostly. A city on a broken floating mesa, Raksha sultans. Also easy access to firedust leads to some pretty tense and exciting moments. Also water, one of the few things Solars can\u2019t just smash through. When the city\u2019s water screws got destroyed that was a huge problem.<br /> <br /> The east one near Vaneha was just kind of standard I guess. It wasn\u2019t even bland it was just okay is just about every respect.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-09-19T09:56:44-07:00","id":1336890,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DrLoveMonkey</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1336854-which-has-been-your-favourite-area-of-3e-creation-how-different-did-the-games-feel?p=1336866#post1336866\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think the worst one was the West game, just because lots of us were really hyped for the sailing and naval combat but that really fell short for us. We never really got that sense of adventure I was looking for but I can\u2019t really articulate why that may be.</div> </div> </div> </div>Do you think this was about the Sailing and Naval Combar rules (which I haven't really used) or just the area, setting, story, etc?<br /> <br /> When I first played Exalted what, 12 years ago maybe, our Dragonblood game was in the West, then our Solar game moved to the West, then we played another Dragonblood game in the West... anyway, we got tired of the West and never went back, so I've not played 3rd ed in the West. Obviously as the book hasn't been released,<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I will say that having a boat that gave us easy access to many separated island cultures was cool though. </div> </div> </div>So as an ST, I've run two (non-Exalted) games where the PCs had their own ships, and on the one hand it's a great opportunity for a variety of really different and interesting cultures. On the other hand, it can be really difficult because the PCs have so much choice about where to go. And while it may be a long time for them to get there in-game, out-of-game it's 5 minutes so if they suddenly decide to go somewhere you didn't expect, you've got to come up with it quickly. Even if they decide at the end of session to go somewhere different, it's a lot more difficult than when they're in a very definite sandbox.<br /> And it also makes it much more difficult to come up with interesting NPCs for them to interact with if they keep leaving them for new places. You can do NPCs on the ship, but that tends to mean they're allies/servants of the PCs, whereas if you want recurring enemies, or rival frenemy monarchs<br /> <br /> One thing I found is that it's not so bad if they're in a particular distinct area with, say, 5 or 6 big islands/planets/whatever, and then various smaller islands/planets-of-hats they can visit if they like.<br /> When running Rogue Trader, I had them in one particular area of planets where two rival powers were fighting over protectorate planets, and that worked well (the game didn't go well for other reasons, but that thing went well I think; though in the very first session, about half an hour in, before they got there, they suddenly went somewhere I hadn't expected and I suddenly had to pull a whole plot out of my ass based on a throwaway line about pirates). The players had choice about where to go, but generally choosing between 3 or 4 planets, so I could plan them all. And they'd go back later to the same planets sometimes.<br /> Whereas when running Star Wars they could choose between thousands of planets, and I found that really awkward to plot for, and most important make engaging NPCs for (ironically, that game's gone way better than Rogue Trader because the PCs are much better, but I did find making cultures for them to visit and engaging NPCs much harder than Rogue Trader).<br /> <br /> Saying that, if I go back to island-hopping in Exalted, I did once play a game (this was in 2nd ed, but it would be the same in 3rd ed), where we travelled along between different, interesting, islands-of-the-week. But the ST was able to plan them well because we were in the far north-west and were going a specific route, east to west. We couldn't suddenly decide to turn south or north and go somewhere else, and so the ST always knew where we were going to go.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> The far far north east game was fun in that it was so far from any Dragonblooded power that we could afford to be a lot more cavalier with our essence and artifacts... It also gave us a chance to develop cultures relatively unaffected by the shadow of the Scarlett Empire. </div> </div> </div>I've found the same with my own game, which is north of Iscomay (it's on the peninsula right at the top-right of Mela's Fangs, on the map of Creation).<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> The east one near Vaneha was just kind of standard I guess. It wasn\u2019t even bland it was just okay is just about every respect. </div> </div> </div>I noticed Vaneha seems the second-most popular location, after Nexus. I assume due to the Japanese aesthetics.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-09-23T11:58:17-07:00","id":1337521,"title":"","content":"I just remembered I forgot to respond to this thread, this post is just here to remind me to do so when I get back to a computer.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-09-23T12:21:51-07:00","id":1337526,"title":"","content":"I'm really enjoying the blank canvas currently provided by the Dreaming Sea. Only one of the games I'm in takes place there but that has a way of being the &quot;leave your expectations at the door&quot; locale.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Sword of Creation</a> a hub for Exalted related content</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","name":"Lioness","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7_2.png","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5443"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-09-23T15:06:28-07:00","id":1337540,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lioness</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1336854-which-has-been-your-favourite-area-of-3e-creation-how-different-did-the-games-feel?p=1337526#post1337526\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm really enjoying the blank canvas currently provided by the Dreaming Sea. Only one of the games I'm in takes place there but that has a way of being the &quot;leave your expectations at the door&quot; locale.</div> </div> </div> </div>Huh, that surprises me. Of the four corners, the Dreaming Sea felt, while new, the most developed. Prasad has quite a lot of stuff written up for it, and its rivals Ysyr and Volivat have a reasonable amount, and there's various other cities like Palanquin, not to mention the Gigants of Dis, Backbenders, etc.<br /> <br /> Still, it is pretty big, and there's all those Wyld islands and stuff. I can definitely see it being different to expectations for people who've played Exalted for a long time, as I assume your playgroup has.<br /> <br /> I was tempted by the Dreaming Sea, but most of my players had done a game there, so I went for the North-East in the end, which basically has Iscomay and... that's it. So I felt that was almost a completely blank slate.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-09-23T17:06:19-07:00","id":1337557,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1336854-which-has-been-your-favourite-area-of-3e-creation-how-different-did-the-games-feel?p=1336890#post1336890\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Do you think this was about the Sailing and Naval Combar rules (which I haven't really used) or just the area, setting, story, etc?</div> </div> </div> </div>I think the two might be somewhat inseparable for me. Of course there are awesome islands large enough for entire campaigns, but something about the West just screams epic sail adventure to me, even if the game isn't permanently on the sea. So when the navy mechanics just totally fall apart it kills it the same way that intrigue in high castle would fall apart with terrible social rules implementation.<br /> <br /> To be fair, I don't hate the sail rules in general, it's just that there isn't anything even remotely, even in numbers, that can match a Solar and it's just 2e all over again.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1336854-which-has-been-your-favourite-area-of-3e-creation-how-different-did-the-games-feel?p=1336890#post1336890\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So as an ST, I've run two (non-Exalted) games where the PCs had their own ships, and on the one hand it's a great opportunity for a variety of really different and interesting cultures. On the other hand, it can be really difficult because the PCs have so much choice about where to go. And while it may be a long time for them to get there in-game, out-of-game it's 5 minutes so if they suddenly decide to go somewhere you didn't expect, you've got to come up with it quickly. Even if they decide at the end of session to go somewhere different, it's a lot more difficult than when<br /> snip<br /> Saying that, if I go back to island-hopping in Exalted, I did once play a game (this was in 2nd ed, but it would be the same in 3rd ed), where we travelled along between different, interesting, islands-of-the-week. But the ST was able to plan them well because we were in the far north-west and were going a specific route, east to west. We couldn't suddenly decide to turn south or north and go somewhere else, and so the ST always knew where we were going to go.</div> </div> </div> </div>Something I do for my campaigns now is something like that. I basically lay out 10-20 locations and just leave adventure seeds for myself in them, that way when players go there I have some stuff already prepared and then I can develop them as the players do their thing. I think if I ever did a West game with recurring NPCs at least half of those NPCs would have to have their own ships or something so they could just appear wherever the players were with no warning as well.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1336854-which-has-been-your-favourite-area-of-3e-creation-how-different-did-the-games-feel?p=1336890#post1336890\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I noticed Vaneha seems the second-most popular location, after Nexus. I assume due to the Japanese aesthetics.</div> </div> </div> </div>Actually the game I ran was set in my own nation just near Vaneha, where a war was being threatened as Vaneha maybe was trying to expand again. One of the reasons I picked it was because Vaneha was a threat, but not one that couldn't be reasoned with, and it was out far enough that the Realm wouldn't factor too much into the politics. You could actually have some interactions without that shadow looming too much.<br /> <br /> Which isn't to say I don't like the Realm how it is, I like that it's so pervasive. It can be annoying, but it's annoying in that way that makes it feel real. It's like the impressive power and reach of the Realm is actually oppressing my games in real life and driving me out deeper into the Threshold.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1121,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","user":"DrLoveMonkey","date":". 09-23-2019, 08:10 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-09-24T01:31:35-07:00","id":1337604,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DrLoveMonkey</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1336854-which-has-been-your-favourite-area-of-3e-creation-how-different-did-the-games-feel?p=1337557#post1337557\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think the two might be somewhat inseparable for me. Of course there are awesome islands large enough for entire campaigns, but something about the West just screams epic sail adventure to me, even if the game isn't permanently on the sea. So when the navy mechanics just totally fall apart it kills it the same way that intrigue in high castle would fall apart with terrible social rules implementation.<br /> <br /> To be fair, I don't hate the sail rules in general, it's just that there isn't anything even remotely, even in numbers, that can match a Solar and it's just 2e all over again.</div> </div> </div> </div>I guess the Naval Combat rules are fairly straightforward and simple compared to the combat rules. It's not quite just &quot;make an opposed roll&quot;, but it's closer to that than normal combat is. In which case, I assume that non-Solars are just continually, utterly overwhelmed by Solar Sail for the whole naval combat, thus you never feel like you're challenged? I haven't used it myself.<br /> How are DB captains against Solars?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Something I do for my campaigns now is something like that. I basically lay out 10-20 locations and just leave adventure seeds for myself in them, that way when players go there I have some stuff already prepared and then I can develop them as the players do their thing. </div> </div> </div>Probably a good idea. But I find it hard to do that many interesting locations. With non-ship-based games, I can do more like 5 or 6 locations, and they can all have some weight behind them.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I think if I ever did a West game with recurring NPCs at least half of those NPCs would have to have their own ships or something so they could just appear wherever the players were with no warning as well. </div> </div> </div>That's what I did with recurring villains in Rogue Trader. But it works better for some character types than others.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> it was out far enough that the Realm wouldn't factor too much into the politics. You could actually have some interactions without that shadow looming too much. </div> </div> </div>This is pretty much why I set my game in the far North-East; there's an expansionist empire (Iscomay), but for E1 characters it's not so overwhelming. They've actually been fighting a single Dragon of troops with its 10 Dragonblood, and they've found it fairly hard; they've killed 4 of the Dragonblood, but lost between them an eye, an arm, and a Changing Moon.<br /> So I'd hate to see how they'd do against a whole Realm Legion. Maybe they can do that at Essence 3.<br /> (Actually, our Essence 5 characters are going to be fighting 3 Realm Legions in a story arc or two... and I'm not optimistic about our chances.)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":2402,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","user":"The Wizard of Oz","date":". 09-24-2019, 05:00 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-09-24T02:38:43-07:00","id":1337607,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1336854-which-has-been-your-favourite-area-of-3e-creation-how-different-did-the-games-feel?p=1337540#post1337540\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Huh, that surprises me. Of the four corners, the Dreaming Sea felt, while new, the most developed. Prasad has quite a lot of stuff written up for it, and its rivals Ysyr and Volivat have a reasonable amount, and there's various other cities like Palanquin, not to mention the Gigants of Dis, Backbenders, etc.<br /> <br /> Still, it is pretty big, and there's all those Wyld islands and stuff. I can definitely see it being different to expectations for people who've played Exalted for a long time, as I assume your playgroup has.<br /> <br /> I was tempted by the Dreaming Sea, but most of my players had done a game there, so I went for the North-East in the end, which basically has Iscomay and... that's it. So I felt that was almost a completely blank slate.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, most of the game thus far has taken place in Y'danna which is a complete blank slate. But even those other places aren't burdened by years of questionable canon which can make the locations feel a lot smaller by reducing them to singular obvious hooks.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Sword of Creation</a> a hub for Exalted related content</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","name":"Lioness","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7_2.png","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5443"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-09-24T03:21:10-07:00","id":1337611,"title":"","content":"That's true actually, a lot of it is just the paragraph in the Core rather than 2 previous editions worth of books.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-09-24T10:14:15-07:00","id":1337654,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1336854-which-has-been-your-favourite-area-of-3e-creation-how-different-did-the-games-feel?p=1337604#post1337604\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I guess the Naval Combat rules are fairly straightforward and simple compared to the combat rules. It's not quite just &amp;quot;make an opposed roll&amp;quot;, but it's closer to that than normal combat is. In which case, I assume that non-Solars are just continually, utterly overwhelmed by Solar Sail for the whole naval combat, thus you never feel like you're challenged? I haven't used it myself.<br /> How are DB captains against Solars?</div> </div> </div> </div>I haven\u2019t used the new DB PC rules for it yet, but my suspicion is they won\u2019t help much. With just 4m of two Essence 2 charms the Solar can double 9s, disappear 1s, and have opponent\u2019s 1s count as their 10s, as well as automatically defeating a ram maneuver. That\u2019s just the start too, I don\u2019t think DBs will be able to keep up. We didn\u2019t have DBs when we were doing this campaign either, so for our campaign is was even more one sided.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1336854-which-has-been-your-favourite-area-of-3e-creation-how-different-did-the-games-feel?p=1337604#post1337604\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This is pretty much why I set my game in the far North-East; there's an expansionist empire (Iscomay), but for E1 characters it's not so overwhelming. They've actually been fighting a single Dragon of troops with its 10 Dragonblood, and they've found it fairly hard; they've killed 4 of the Dragonblood, but lost between them an eye, an arm, and a Changing Moon.<br /> So I'd hate to see how they'd do against a whole Realm Legion. Maybe they can do that at Essence 3.<br /> (Actually, our Essence 5 characters are going to be fighting 3 Realm Legions in a story arc or two... and I'm not optimistic about our chances.)</div> </div> </div> </div>I really like the legion you posted, it gives a good impression of the sheer scale and diversity of a deployed legion. Especially since full real Realm legions tend to have more along the lines of 50 Dragonblooded.<br /> <br /> With that said that three legion throwdown with 150 DBs, probably an Essence 5 general, and like 30,000 soldiers sounds like bad news. Then again you\u2019re Essence 5, something I\u2019ve never personally seen in 3e, so you might be just fine.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-09-24T10:36:12-07:00","id":1337659,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I haven\u2019t used the new DB PC rules for it yet, but my suspicion is they won\u2019t help much. With just 4m of two Essence 2 charms the Solar can double 9s, disappear 1s, and have opponent\u2019s 1s count as their 10s, as well as automatically defeating a ram maneuver. That\u2019s just the start too, I don\u2019t think DBs will be able to keep up </div> </div> </div>Doesn't sound like it. They can do some interesting things, but in opposed rolls I can't see them beating that.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I really like the legion you posted, it gives a good impression of the sheer scale and diversity of a deployed legion. Especially since full real Realm legions tend to have more along the lines of 50 Dragonblooded. </div> </div> </div>Well, Dragon rather than Legion. But thanks.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> With that said that three legion throwdown with 150 DBs, probably an Essence 5 general, and like 30,000 soldiers sounds like bad news. Then again you\u2019re Essence 5, something I\u2019ve never personally seen in 3e, so you might be just fine. </div> </div> </div>I think we'd be in with a good chance if the Dawn with every single War charm and the Solar Sorcerer worked together. The Legions are coming from different directions. My PC tried to encourage the PCs to attack the city where the first Legion was stationed before the others could reach the area, but no-one else was up for it. And even now, I think if we went together, in unison, we could defeat one maybe.<br /> But the two most useful characters for this hate each other and won't work together. And some of the other characters don't consider the Realm a big threat, because the Realm claimed they were only going to attack the sorceress and leave everyone else alone.<br /> <br /> But we'll see. The game's on hiatus currently, so it probably won't be until early next year that we get into the Realm attacking. All they've done so far is send a couple of Wyld Hunts after PCs and killed some of our Sorceress's bound second-circle demons.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":2402,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","user":"The Wizard of Oz","date":". 09-24-2019, 01:38 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-14T06:27:57-07:00","id":1341245,"title":"","content":"Having rules for Dragon-Blooded PCs can in some ways limits their utility as NPCs if you don't escape a certain mindset.<br /> <br /> One of the most impressive things the DB QC could do was that their excellency also allowed them to reroll (essence) dice because it meant a Solar's dice tricks were likely to be necessary against a Terrestrial Exalted elder on the top of their game capable of matching or slightly exceeding their dice cap. Splitting it up gave more things for Dragon-Blooded PCs to work on but made it harder to tell when someone like Mnemon could dial things up to 11 and if she even should if WFHW didn't provide a canonical method in this instance.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Sword of Creation</a> a hub for Exalted related content</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","name":"Lioness","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7_2.png","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5443"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-14T10:47:11-07:00","id":1341279,"title":"","content":"As a storyteller I\u2019m definitely opposed to using PC generation rules for NPC antagonists. Especially if multiples of them are showing up at once, keeping all their dicepools and charms in your head at one time is really hard and not usually worth it. It often deflates characters from a numbers standpoint, but inflated their versatility, so it comes out about even but with way more work.<br /> <br /> Like the Abyssal QC has a charm that\u2019s kind of Hungry Tiger Technique except better. It\u2019s helpful for making them dangerous but keeping them in check as well. You don\u2019t have some perfectly constructed abyssal Dusk caste killing your whole circle.<br /> <br /> I actually think we could do with a few more Solar and Abyssal QCs in the antagonist sections.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}